WEBVTT

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.590
Welcome to my castle!

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.870
Don't be rude.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.940
He's an important guest.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:34.860
Be good now.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.590
Well, please step in.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.200
You know something about Keisuke?

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.320
Of course.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.200
I know what he's been busy with lately.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.210
Busy with?

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.710
He slaughtered about a dozen other
participants in the Neutral Zone.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.800
Not something an ordinary
person would be capable of.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.880
Seems he responds well to Line.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.640
Stop twisting your words.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:06.330
Wasn't that what he wanted?

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.320
Or is what you want the
only thing that matters?

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.060
What do you mean?

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.900
I wonder if you want to save your friend...

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.950
With my help, it could be possible.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.500
However, there's something I want in return.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.730
What is it?

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.130
Some of your blood.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.440
What do you need it for?

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.840
Anyhow, please step in.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.780
Let's have a nice chat, shall we?

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.990
Distractions day after day, it's always something

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.990
Meutsuri Shiteru Hibi Are Kore

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.130
and no one has even realized that

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.140
I see the crimson trailing down your cold skin

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.140
Awadatsu Hada wo Tsutai Ochiru CRIMSON

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:20.330
Why do you want another punishment?

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:20.330
Why do you want Atarashii Batsu wo

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.080
The sweet fragrances that are drifting about

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.080
Tadayou Amai Kaori wo Tada

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:29.640
I just want to leave them be

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:29.640
Asobasete Itai Dake Nano sa

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:37.320
Someone hurry up and shoot me

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:37.320
Dareka Boku wo Hayaku Uchinuite yo

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:42.470
Show me a gunshot strong enough to make a hole

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:42.470
Show me Kantsuushita Juusou Ana ga Aku Hodo

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.940
I crush my thorny grip

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.940
Toge Darake no GRIP Nigiritsubushite

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:52.710
and load bullets that look like ripe flowerbuds

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:52.710
Osanai Mada Tsubomi no You na Dangan de

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.820
Let me shoot through the soul

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.820
Let me, shot through the soul

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.770
and dye it rose

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.770
Bara-iro ni Somare

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.430
What do you know about Line so far?

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.730
Just start from the beginning.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.680
This is important to the
main question at hand.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:30.050
It's a dangerous drug that drives people mad.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.370
Line unleashes the latent
abilities in humans!

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:38.070
It's like a treasure from the gods!

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:46.080
Here in Toshima, only me, Il Re and
Premier know about its true character.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.040
Premier?

00:03:55.510 --> 00:04:01.590
In the days before the war, the government
planned Project Nicole for creating the strongest soldier.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.560
For this purpose, they created the top
secret private research facility called ENED.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.010
They assembled the most talented specialists
to conduct high level research.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.370
And finally, they created a miracle!

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.120
From the blood of a single
subject named Premier,

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.330
they discovered a substance that could
greatly improve the capabilities of the human body.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:30.920
The researchers who discovered this unknown
substance named it after the project.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.340
They called it Nicole.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.420
This was the raw material for Line.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.850
It was the most well-kept
secret in the country.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:43.560
And due to unfortunate circumstances that
took place, that secret is now in my hands.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.960
And also, in you.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:46.810
In me?

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.240
Unfortunately I can't disclose that
information until I'm certain.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.980
I have all the reason to believe
that you were ENED's test subject.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.360
I've never heard of ENED before.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.320
People who are highly compatible
with Nicole are extremely rare.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:06.290
You see, with the government's help,
ENED collected a lot of orphans.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.960
Me and Keisuke were in a regular orphanage.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.340
Government or army have nothing...

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.550
My name is Emma and this is Gwen.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:22.510
We'd like you to think of
us as being unimportant.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:23.970
The army...

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.060
Apparently, the children who were deemed
unsuitable had their memories erased

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.760
and were returned to the institutions
from where they came.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.500
Maybe your friend was one
of these subjects, too.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.430
We were test subjects?

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.130
I have no doubt.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.030
But it looks like you were the only
one who was a little different.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.740
What are you talking about?

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:49.860
Your blood neutralizes Nicole.
Or in other words, Line.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:50.750
Neutralizes?

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.720
Then why did the ones
who tasted my blood die?

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.850
Die?

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.520
Oh, you're talking about the
addict who took in your blood.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:09.680
His body strongly rejected it.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:14.430
You see, neutralizing Nicole produces toxins.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.280
I guess his body couldn't withstand it.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.280
But with the correct methods,
you can stop the poison.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:26.620
You have something miraculous in your blood.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.370
I could save Keisuke with my blood?

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:31.120
Well, how about it?

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.260
Won't you cooperate with me for
the sake of saving your friend?

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.800
All right.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.230
Akira!

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.960
Where did you run off to?

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:17.140
You know I'll find you...

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:18.370
Akira.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.870
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:29.880
It's okay.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.500
Naturally, my prediction was spot on.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.190
So how do I save Keisuke?

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.090
I need some time.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.990
I have to find a safe way to use it.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:44.490
How long is it gonna take?

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:47.050
I'll hurry, of course.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:51.540
In the mean time, would you like to
rest? I had a room prepared for you.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.060
Nah, that's fine.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:53.800
I'll come back later.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.050
Please wait!

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.620
It would be bad if something happened to you!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:06.730
Try to understand your own worth.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:13.570
You had this planned right
from the start, didn't you?!

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.720
How beautiful.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:19.220
That defiant look in your
eyes gives me the thrills.

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:23.530
Now, let me show you to your room.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.500
Don't touch me!

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:33.570
Damn.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.120
You people!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:38.830
Lower your weapons!

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:41.110
Stop it!

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.050
Apologize for your rudeness!

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:46.530
D-Don't you want to save your friend?!

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.100
You were being so confident.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.580
You already know how to
use my blood, don't you?

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.000
I-I don't!

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:54.930
I swear!

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.720
It takes time to figure out!

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.200
Quickly!

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.530
Catch him!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:14.500
Don't shoot!

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.990
Capture him alive!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.380
Whatever you do, don't kill him!

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:18.210
Wait!

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.430
Akira!

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.820
Project Nicole.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.580
Akira?

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.450
How long have you been there?

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:13.960
I just got here.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.570
Speak up, man.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.640
I had something serious to take care of.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.970
Geez, so unlike you.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.070
You sound like Rin.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.300
By the way, did you find Keisuke?

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:28.150
Well...

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.000
What is it?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:30.970
Oh, no...

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.530
Do you understand this?

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:36.180
It's like you're giving me new intel.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.030
Let's see...

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.120
This is...

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.780
Chemical composition.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.550
Where did you get this paper?

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.430
Gramps?

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:57.050
Sorry.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.550
You want to save Keisuke, right?

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:02.190
Yeah.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:07.100
From what I can see here,
your blood is too dangerous.

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:09.190
You mustn't use it.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.320
But...

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:13.700
Arbitro said there's a way to use it safely.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.340
It's not that simple.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:20.310
Didn't you say that you're just an
information broker? How come you know this stuff?!

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:25.630
There's no easy way to put it.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:30.420
I was once a researcher for ENED.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.080
I was just a low ranked one.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.960
Arbitro was...

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:37.770
I guess you could call him a colleague.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:38.990
At ENED?

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:42.520
This is gonna sound harsh,

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:46.310
but saving a person who has
taken Line is impossible.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.230
That's the reality of it.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.670
But I have to do something.

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:52.920
This isn't a game!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:57.840
Arbitro told me that if my blood is digested
by someone who's taken Line, it'll create poison.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.370
That's correct.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:05.160
But if we can do something about that
poison, it'll be possible to save Keisuke.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:09.000
But what if that doesn't work? Then what?

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.050
What would you do if Keisuke dies?

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.610
I want to save Keisuke.

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.720
Stay calm, Akira!

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.520
Are you going to look for Arbitro?

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.350
If you want to leave this place,
at least wait until morning.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:26.440
It's dangerous right now.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:29.700
But why...?

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:32.730
Why Keisuke?

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:35.750
Why is my blood like this?

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.200
Calm down, Akira!

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:40.370
I know it's painful, but it's the truth!

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:42.490
There's no one who has
recovered from taking Line!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.930
That drug is of the devil!

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.870
Is that why you're telling me to give up?!

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.880
Didn't you see how Keisuke
has totally changed?

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.040
Is there really...

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.340
...nothing that I can do?

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.360
There's no hospital or police here.

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.790
Strangers don't care if you die alone.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.060
That's the kind of town Toshima is.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:09.980
But

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.480
Keisuke is...

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:17.680
Let me treat your injuries for now.

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:26.780
Am I just imagining things or is
the main force being really noisy?

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.120
So you noticed.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:32.890
Seems that the rumor about those guys from
the Nikko Group making their move was true.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.690
The CFC and the Nikko Group are just facades.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.790
They used to be symbols for this country, but now
they're talking about taking control of the capital.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:45.350
Their true goal is to capture n in Toshima.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:46.860
We must hurry.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:48.260
We must not be defeated!

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:06.420
It was a night like this back then, too.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:43.080
Shiki!

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:46.220
Where are you?!

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:51.760
Is it really you?

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:06.350
I'm not letting you get away today.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:08.890
I'll make you use your sword.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:24.070
How many times are you going
to show off your clumsiness?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.110
Shut up!

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.490
Draw your sword!

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:30.910
Or do you think I'm not worth it?

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:36.080
I'm not interested in your
eternally cliche sentimentality.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.550
You've always been like that.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:45.020
You've never had the slightest interest
in your worthless little brother.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.660
But for me,

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.140
you were the big brother who I was
proud of and aspired to be like.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.600
How could I be so stupid?

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:56.410
We had different mothers,
but I still believed in you.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.880
It was my goal to be like you.

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:02.650
That's why my friends...

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.530
I'll never forgive myself.

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:07.530
And I won't forgive you either!

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:21.710
I will kill you for what
you did to my friends.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.180
I swear I'll kill you...

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:30.770
No matter what it takes.

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:34.430
Trash should know their place.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:38.930
I'm not interested in assisting with suicide.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:39.600
Get out of my sight.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.250
Stay down there and curse your own weakness.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.210
Wait!

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.140
Hey, aren't I amazing?

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.840
Isn't this how you wanted me to be?

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.310
Akiraaa!

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.150
You okay, Akira?

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.690
Sorry about that earlier.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.540
I was acting childish, too.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:19.120
I was a bit too surprised.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:22.620
You'll have to decide whether or
not you believe in me for yourself.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:24.140
You must be tired.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.360
You can rest here if you don't mind.

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:27.500
Yeah.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.090
Here.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.920
I bet you haven't been getting enough food.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.050
Consider it resupplying.

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.510
This place's gonna turn
into a battlefield soon.

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:36.890
You mean Toshima?

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.610
Yeah.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:41.940
The CFC and the Nikko Group
are mobilizing the army.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:45.610
A smart guy would've made
preparations to escape long ago.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:50.370
I don't want you to die in vain.

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.320
You should escape alone.

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:55.280
I can't leave Keisuke behind.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:58.370
I see.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:04.420
But why did a guy like you
come here in the first place?

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:06.210
To clear away false charges.

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.250
False charges?

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:10.780
They arrested me and blamed me
for a murder I didn't commit.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:14.270
They told me to go and defeat Il Re if I
didn't want to spend the rest of my life in prison.

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:18.720
I think they probably got the
idea from the military people.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.100
So that's how you got into this.

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:27.230
And Keisuke was worried about
me and followed me here.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.650
Don't make it sound like it was your fault.

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:34.460
Keisuke himself made the
decision to take part in Igra.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:38.120
But I'm the one who drove
Keisuke to use Line.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:42.220
I've always been relying on his kindness.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.610
I took him for granted.

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:49.210
I never thought about his feelings.

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:53.140
I didn't even want to know about them.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:57.090
I'm the one who drove him that far.

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:00.600
It's not that easy to understand
another person's feelings.

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:04.060
It can be difficult to convey your thoughts.

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:08.060
But this time you have to do it.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.510
Don't give up.

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:15.990
Didn't Keisuke say that it was
thanks to you he came to Toshima?

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.660
He was betting his life on you.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:21.960
If that's the case, then that's all the more
reason for you to make things clear to him.

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:25.000
The way you're feeling now.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:29.540
The most important thing now isn't what's in
your blood or how to use it to save Keisuke.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:30.350
Akira,

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:32.460
the most important thing is your heart.

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:36.970
If you really want to save Keisuke,
you have to bring him here.

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.590
I'll help you escape.

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:39.730
Gramps...

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:40.950
Rin, too.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.160
Daddy!

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:26.100
Are you testing me again?

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:30.480
Give me a break...

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:42.820
Sup.

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:48.220
Why the long face?

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:50.250
You don't need to be afraid of me.

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:53.250
Keisuke.

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:54.650
What?

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:56.670
I've been looking for you.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.360
I really wanted

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:00.680
to meet you.

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:20.980
start shifted back 10

00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:30.980
We embraced, as if drifting through nothingness

00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:30.980
We embrace Kuuhaku o Tadayou You ni

00:22:31.970 --> 00:22:40.650
You smeared out my heart with your overwhelming existence

00:22:31.970 --> 00:22:40.650
Nazoru Sonzai de Kokoro o Nuritsubushite

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:49.280
The faces you show me
were always of a fleeting love

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:49.280
Ukabu Hyoujou wa Tebanashi no Ai

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:59.050
You accepted me solely for my sake, not your own

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:59.050
Boku no Tame Dake ni Uketekurete Tane

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:03.390
I miss you

00:23:03.590 --> 00:23:10.450
Our bonds used to be so strong

00:23:03.590 --> 00:23:10.450
Fukaku Tsunagatteta Nante

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:19.550
But how can I ask you to understand me now?

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:19.550
Imasara Douyatte Wakatte Moraeru Darou

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:28.750
I'm alone in darkness without your comfort

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:28.750
Kurai Sekai de Hagureta Mama de

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:37.980
I brushed off your existence as a mere person

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:37.980
Kimi no Koto o Ozanari ni Shiteta

00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:45.650
Yet your kindness still protects me

00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:45.650
Yasashisa ni Mamorarete

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:52.110
Hey, Akira.

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:54.620
For me you're like a hero.

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:56.900
I've always been following you.

00:23:57.310 --> 00:23:58.570
Annoying, isn't it?

00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:02.580
So don't look at me like that!

00:24:01.880 --> 00:24:04.510
Episode 9

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:04.280
Akiraaa!
